Z||000000||bpfiero||04-17-2001||10:44 PM||||Driving home from work today,  everything is great until  I started to slow down for my exit,  I herd a weird creeking sound coming from my rear (passenger side) tire only on every rotation. wooooolf pause  ...... woooolf  pause........ect  it's Not the brakes...put in a new axle 5-7 months ago so I'm sure it's not that. If antbody had this happen to them please let me know that its an easy fix<P>Thanks<P>Bpfiero <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cuz2.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-18-2001||10:09 AM||||Well first guess would be that you have new brake pads that are rubbing against the rotor.  New brake linings will do that until they are worn the way the rotor wants them to.<P>If you say they are good, then I dont have any other suggestions.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||04-18-2001||10:28 AM||||when sitting still without the engine running press hard on the brake and let it go a few times and let me know if you hear the creak||||reg||6
